--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
1. THIRD-PARTY CONTENT IS NOT LICENSED HERE
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

The calculator this repository packages is not its author's original work.

The calculator's design, keypad layout, calculation logic and visual styling
originate from https://baiiplusfinancialcalculator.com/. The files
`upstream_raw/styles.css`, `upstream_raw/script.js`, `upstream_raw/index.html`
and the webfonts are that site's files, redistributed here unmodified. Copyright
in them belongs to their author, who is not affiliated with this repository.

The MIT licence above applies ONLY to the work added here: the build pipeline
under `tools/`, the offline overrides and behaviour patches under `src/`, and the
documentation. It makes no claim over the upstream files and cannot grant you
rights that the upstream author has not granted.

If you are the rights holder of the upstream content and want it removed, open
an issue and it will be taken down.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
2. NOT AFFILIATED WITH TEXAS INSTRUMENTS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

BA II Plus and BA II Plus Professional are trademarks of Texas Instruments
Incorporated. This project is not produced by, endorsed by, sponsored by or
affiliated with Texas Instruments. It is an independent web emulation, and so is
the site it was packaged from.

--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
3. NOT FINANCIAL ADVICE — VERIFY YOUR RESULTS
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------

This is a study and reference tool. Financial calculations carry consequences:
an exam answer, a valuation, a loan decision.

The calculator's behaviour was verified against the source site, not against a
physical BA II Plus, and the two are known to differ in the ways documented in
the README. Its arithmetic is ordinary floating-point arithmetic and is not
suitable for exact decimal work.

Nothing produced by this software is financial, investment, accounting, tax or
legal advice. Check anything you intend to rely on against a device or a source
you trust. You are responsible for the results you use.

